+# Spec: `use-waitgroup-go` — support loops after `wg.Add`
+
+Status: implemented
+
+## Objective
+`use-waitgroup-go` should also flag `wg.Add(n)` when it's followed by a loop
+(`for range ...`, `for ... range ...` or a classic `for`) whose body launches a
+goroutine that calls `wg.Done()`. Each iteration's goroutine can then be
+replaced with `wg.Go(...)`. Source: kubernetes-sigs/kueue#9892.
+
+```go
+wg.Add(int(jobs)) // MATCH
+for range int(jobs) {
+	go func() {
+		defer wg.Done()
+		doSomething()
+	}()
+}
+```
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- A `wg.Add(...)` statement followed (in the same block) by a `for`/`range`
+  statement whose body has a top-level `go func(){ ... wg.Done() ... }()` is
+  reported with the existing message.
+- At most one failure per `wg.Add`.
+- Behaviour that already exists stays the same, including the Go < 1.25 skip.
+- Not reported: loops whose goroutines don't call `wg.Done`, and goroutines that
+  run a named function rather than a function literal.
+
+## Commands
+- `go test ./test/ -run TestUseWaitGroupGo`
+- `go test ./...`
+
+## Structure / style
+- Code: `rule/use_waitgroup_go.go`. Fixtures: `testdata/go1.25/use_waitgroup_go.go`
+  (matches) and `testdata/use_waitgroup_go.go` (go < 1.25, no matches).
+- Follow the repo's existing style; no new dependencies.
+
+## Testing
+Add fixture cases for `for range n`, `for i := range n` and the classic `for`,
+plus negative cases: a loop with no `wg.Done`, and a loop that runs a named function.
+
+## Boundaries
+- Always: keep the name-based heuristic (`wg`) and leave the failure message as is.
+- Never: add type-checking requirements or change other rules.
